      "problem": "What is the reciprocal of $2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given mixed number to an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5} = \\dfrac{(2\\times 5)+2}{5}=\\dfrac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nTo find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}12}{\\color{red}5} \\quad\\rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{blue}12}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $2\\,\\dfrac{2}{5}$ is $\\dfrac{5}{12}.$",
